  "worked_solution": "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are two matrices from $E,$ then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}\n$$\n\n is a diagonal matrix. This matrix belongs to $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A$ is an element of $E,$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\nkA\n$$\n\n is a diagonal matrix. This matrix belongs to $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"",
